From eaff9e136b6c4597539a4949488d75ad93b5be83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Khaled <khaledchoucri@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 15:46:37 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] POC-10d: FOLDER screen fixes - grouped rows, copy limits
 shown, candy unlock rule

- Folder page groups chips (move + code) with a quantity; every page shows each
  move's copies in the folder against its MB limit (LIMIT column, panel line,
  clear message when the limit stops an add)
- Candy shop: a move unlocks at the level the Pokemon learns it (only an
  evolved form's level-1 moves need the move's MB in level) - a Lv5 Wingull now
  unlocks Water Gun; moves still to come are listed greyed with their level

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FbWSqvcg6G5Gpw6ynvR5tJ
---
 src/pkbn/folder_ui.c | 197 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 153 insertions(+), 44 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/pkbn/folder_ui.c b/src/pkbn/folder_ui.c
index 14984ec..417bc6c 100644
--- a/src/pkbn/folder_ui.c
+++ b/src/pkbn/folder_ui.c
@@ -5,8 +5,12 @@
 //   FOLDER  the chips battles draw from. A: take a chip out. SELECT: auto-build again. B: save and leave.
 //   PACK    every chip you own. A: put one in the folder. START: use a PP UP on it (+1 copy).
 //           SELECT: use a PP MAX on it (copies of that move up to its cap).
-//   CANDY   chips you can buy with type candy: moves of that type a Pokémon you own has reached by level-up
-//           (and at least the move's MB in level). A: buy (cost MB/4). SELECT: change the code (+2 candy).
+//   CANDY   chips you can buy with type candy: moves of that type a Pokémon you own has reached by level-up.
+//           (An evolved form's level-1 moves - Raichu's Thunderbolt - need the move's MB in level.) Moves your
+//           Pokémon will learn later are listed greyed with the level they need. A: buy (cost MB/4).
+//           SELECT: change the code (+2 candy).
+// Lists are grouped by chip (move + code) with quantities, sorted by type; every row shows the copy limit
+// (BN6: how many copies of one chip a folder may hold, set by its MB).
